breaking_changes.Adaptation_method:
To suppress the error and maintain legacy behavior, add '.allowExcessArguments()' to your command setup.

Before 13.0.0:
program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.action((options) => {
  console.log(program.args);
});

After 13.0.0 (to avoid error):
program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.allowExcessArguments();
program.action((options) => {
  console.log(program.args);
});

Alternatively, declare the expected arguments using '.argument(...)'.

Only use supported option flag formats during Option construction. For single-character options, use one character after single '-', or use double '--' for long options.

Before 13.0.0 (was allowed, now error):
new Option('-ab, --foo');

After 13.0.0:
// Split into separate Option declarations for each flag, or use correct syntax
new Option('-a, --foo');
new Option('-b, --bar');
